Package: mediaPlanCopula
Type: Package
Title: Copula-Based Exposure Distributions for Mixed Media Plans
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Manuel J.", family = "Sánchez-Franco",
           email = "majesus@us.es", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8042-3550"))
Description: Computes the distribution of the number of contacts, the reach and
    the average opportunities to see of a media plan that mixes vehicles with a
    bounded number of insertions (Beta-Binomial) and vehicles with an unbounded
    stream of impressions (Negative Binomial, as a Poisson-Gamma mixture). The
    vehicles are linked by a Gaussian copula on their latent exposure
    propensities, whose correlation matrix is calibrated pairwise, by
    numerical quadrature, to reproduce the observed duplication of the
    first insertions. Copula models for marketing data are described by
    Danaher and Smith (2011) <doi:10.1287/mksc.1090.0491>; multivariate media
    exposure models by Danaher (1991) <doi:10.1177/002224379102800311>.
